<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Occupation of Araucanía</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1861">1861</a>–<a href="/years/1883">1883</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Pacification of Araucanía</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Occupation of Araucanía was the Chilean military campaign and settlement that brought the independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> lands south of the Biobío river under Chilean rule between 1861 and 1883. Forts and towns were founded, Mapuche lands were confiscated and their people confined to reservations, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-the-desert">Conquest of the Desert</a> subdued the Mapuche east of the Andes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/occupation-of-araucania.jpg" alt="Occupation of Araucanía" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ccpchile · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fuerte_de_Pur%C3%A9n_Chile.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
